var SPF={"Banshee Wail":"You let out a soul-shattering wail. Each creature in a 30 ft cone that hears it makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it takes 6d10 psychic and is frightened of you, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns to end the fear. On a success it takes 3d10 psychic and is not frightened. Constructs and undead are unaffected.","Beguiling Gift":"You plant a strong suggestion in an item as you hand it to someone. If they accept it willingly, they make a Wisdom save or use the item as intended at their first opportunity: writing with a pen, eating or drinking, wearing clothes, drawing a weapon and so on. After that first use they feel no pull to keep using it or even to keep it.","Borrowing":"By touching a target you gain one of its senses, movement types and speeds, feats, languages, immunities or extraordinary abilities for the duration. The target keeps using it too. An unwilling target prevents this with a Constitution save. The target can be living or dead for no more than 1 minute (a corpse makes no save). You hold only one borrowed power at a time. Higher slots: at slot 5 the duration is 1 hour and the target loses the power for that time.","Circle of Devestation":"You create a ring of destructive energy 10 ft tall and 20 ft in radius around a point you see in range. The area inside is difficult terrain. When you cast and as a bonus action each turn, choose cold, fire, lightning, necrotic or radiant. Creatures and objects that touch the ring, are inside it when it forms, or end their turn inside take 6d6 of that type, or half with a Constitution save. A creature or object reduced to 0 hit points becomes fine ash. At the start of each of your later turns the ring's radius grows by 20 ft, and anything it touches is affected immediately.","Cloying Darkness":"A hand of decaying shadow reaches out. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 2d8 necrotic and makes a Constitution save. On a failure shadow covers its eyes until the start of your next turn, so it treats bright light as dim, dim light as darkness, and darkness as magical darkness. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 1st.","Cosmic Alignment":"You arrange cosmic forces in your favor. Choose a cosmic event from the Comprehension of the Starry Sky ability that affects spellcasting: conjunction, eclipse or nova. Until the next sunrise or 24 hours pass, you cast as if under it. Where the ability asks you to spend insight, you spend your ritual focus instead. You must cast it outdoors, and everyone within 100 miles can tell, as a symbol such as a flaming comet appears in the sky. Conjunction: give one creature disadvantage on a save against one enchantment or illusion spell you cast. Eclipse: when a spell of 5th level or lower you cast deals necrotic damage, reroll up to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one) damage dice and keep the new rolls. Nova: treat one divination spell you cast as if you used a slot one level higher.","Extract Foyson":"You pull the nutrition out of three days' worth of meals and condense it into about a tablespoon of bland flour. Mixed with liquid and drunk, or baked into elven bread, it gives all the original nutritional value for the amount eaten. The original food looks unchanged and still fills, but has no nutrition, and someone eating only that will eventually starve. Higher slots: three more meals' worth per slot level above 1st. If you spend your ritual focus, each day's foyson can take the form of a slice of delicious elven bread.","Hearth Charm":"Flammable material in range burns twice as long as normal for the duration.","Hod's Gift":"The target gains blindsight to a range of 60 ft for the duration. Higher slots: +1 hour per slot level above 5th.","Jotun's Jest":"A weapon or other item in range swells to the size meant for a Gargantuan creature. It weighs 12 times its normal weight and creatures smaller than Gargantuan generally cannot use it well. It keeps all its qualities, including magical powers, and returns to normal when the spell ends.","Loki's Gift":"Your lie turns strangely plausible. You have advantage on Charisma (Deception) checks for whatever you are saying now. If the check fails, the creature knows you tried to manipulate it with magic. If you lie to a creature with a friendly attitude and it fails a Charisma save, you can coax it to reveal a potentially embarrassing secret. The secret can involve wrongdoing or a hidden fear, but not something life-threatening or shameful enough to brand the subject a pariah. The verbal component is the lie you tell.","Risen Road":"You open a glowing portal to the plane of shadow, open for 1 minute, until 10 creatures pass through, or until you collapse it without an action. Stepping through puts you on a shadow road toward a destination within 50 miles or in a direction you name. The road is in ideal condition and you and your companions can travel it safely at a normal pace, but cannot rest: stopping more than 10 minutes ends the spell and drops you in the real world at a random spot within 10 miles of the start. The spell ends 2d6 hours after casting. Then travelers are safely placed near their destination, or 50 miles from the start in the chosen direction. Travelers gain no exhaustion from hours spent on the road. The road then vanishes and anything left behind is lost in shadow. Each casting makes a new road. A temporary road might cross an existing shadow road, allowing encounters with other travelers or monsters or a change of destination. The GM decides the likelihood.","Shadow Realm Gateway":"You draw a chalk circle up to 15 ft across in black chalk and chant for a minute to open a portal into the Shadow Realm. It fills the circle as a vortex of black, and nothing can be seen through it. Anything passing through arrives safely in the Shadow Realm. The portal stays open for one minute or until you lose concentration, and works in both directions any number of times. It can only be cast as a ritual.","Snowblind Stare":"Your eyes glow with bright, cold light that inflicts snow blindness on a creature you target within 30 ft. On a failed Constitution save it suffers the first stage of snow blindness, or the second stage if it already has the first. It recovers as the condition describes.","Wotan's Rede":"You recite a poem in the Northern tongue to gain insight. Your next Intelligence or Charisma check within 1 minute has advantage, and you can add twice your proficiency bonus. At the GM's discretion it can instead give a piece of general advice similar to contact other plane."};
